<title>USA: Central Financial signs new credit pact.</title>
<headline>Central Financial signs new credit pact.</headline>
<dateline>COMMERCE, Calif. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Financial Acceptance Corp Wednesday said it has replaced two existing credit lines with a new $100 million facility via Wells Fargo Bank, a unit of Wells Fargo and Co.</p>
<p>The two lines replaced were a $50 million facility from Wells Fargo and a $60 million facility from several banks with agent Bank of America National Trust and Savings Association, a unit of BankAmerica Corp.</p>
